# Kaggle Notebook environment — copy to .env.kaggle in the project root before uploading.
#
# ── Step 1: Make the project code available on Kaggle ──
#
#   Option A — Clone from GitHub (easiest):
#     Add a setup cell at the top of your notebook, before cell 0:
#       !git clone https://github.com/<you>/fake-news-detection.git /kaggle/working/fake-news-detection
#     The default KAGGLE_PROJECT_ROOT below already points there.
#
#   Option B — Upload as a Kaggle Dataset:
#     1. Create a Kaggle Dataset from the project zip (exclude *.h5 and .git/)
#     2. Add it as input to your notebook
#     3. Set a Kaggle Secret: KAGGLE_PROJECT_ROOT=/kaggle/input/<your-dataset-slug>
#
# ── Step 2: Make the HDF5 data available on Kaggle ──
#   1. Upload coolant_train.h5, coolant_dev.h5, coolant_test.h5 as a Kaggle Dataset
#      (from Drive: MyDrive/Thesis_Final/fake-news-data-for-thesis/processed_data/hdf5/)
#   2. Add the dataset as input to your notebook
#   3. Update DATA_ROOT below to match the mounted path (see slug in notebook URL)
#
# ── Step 3: Handle checkpoint output ──
#   Kaggle input datasets are read-only. Checkpoints write to DATA_ROOT/training/,
#   so DATA_ROOT must be writable. Two options:
#     • Set DATA_ROOT=/kaggle/working and copy the HDF5 files there in a setup cell:
#         !cp /kaggle/input/<hdf5-slug>/processed_data/hdf5/*.h5 /kaggle/working/processed_data/hdf5/
#     • OR override CONFIG["paths"]["checkpoint_root"] in cell 2 to /kaggle/working/checkpoints
#       and keep DATA_ROOT pointing to the read-only input dataset.

# Path where HDF5 input data is mounted (update <slug> to your dataset slug)
DATA_ROOT=/kaggle/input/<your-hdf5-dataset-slug>

# Platform identifier (used by env_utils.py)
PLATFORM=kaggle
